      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# dsh-wsl-service

DeepSeek Harness plugin: Read Windows service state from WSL: list services and inspect one by name.

Part of **[dsh-wsl-kit](https://github.com/173787247/dsh-wsl-kit)**.

[中文说明 → README.zh.md](./README.zh.md)

## Install

```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add github:173787247/dsh-wsl-service
```

## Usage

```
win_services                          # all services
win_services state=running limit=20
win_services name=Spooler             # one service
```

## Notes

Read-only: this plugin lists and inspects services, it does not start or stop them.
`total` counts services matching the filter, which can exceed `listed`.

## Requirements

- Windows with WSL, and DeepSeek Harness running inside it.

## Tests

```sh
npm test
```

The unit tests run anywhere. The live tests are skipped outside WSL.

## Compatibility

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Plugin** | `dsh-wsl-service` **0.1.0** |
| **Minimum dsh** | ≥ **0.1.2** (web UI one-shot `?token=` on Windows relay `:3081`) |
| **Latest verified** | See [dsh-wsl-kit Compatibility](https://github.com/173787247/dsh-wsl-kit#compatibility-2026-09) (currently **`0.2.0-rc.2`**) — single source of truth for the suite |
| **Kit set** | `full` or install alone |

